      "effectContract": {
        "id": "ntilde-kitty-animation-persistent-compose-effect-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "statement": "In a persistent tab, a=c composes a whole source frame onto a destination frame of a retained image as the Kitty protocol specifies, read by paired offscreen captures: with C=1 the destination frame is replaced by the source frame's pixels, alpha included (a half-transparent green frame 4, built on no base, replaces the opaque blue frame 3, so the pane shows the green at its own alpha over the terminal background, where a blend would have shown it over the blue); by default the source is alpha-blended, so the same half-transparent frame blended onto the opaque red root shows the protocol's blend of the two; and compositions the protocol refuses (a missing frame: ENOENT; a rectangle wider than the image, and one frame onto itself with overlapping rectangles: EINVAL) answer exactly those error codes and change nothing (the displayed frame stays the root, and frame 2 is still its own green afterwards). Every other command that expects a Kitty reply returned OK, and each clear passed its fence and left its target blank (a=d success is silent).",
        "primary": "https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/graphics-protocol/#composing-animation-frames",
        "carrierCases": [
          "kitty.animation.compose-replace-blend",
          "kitty.animation.compose-refused"
        ],
